<title>UK: CU up on fresh ABN bid talk.</title>
<headline>CU up on fresh ABN bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Commercial Union Plc (CU) put on 15-1/2p to 673-1/2p on renewed speculation that ABN AMRO Holding NV may be interested in buying the company, dealers and analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a story that was about last year and you can see the logic with CU about number four in the Dutch market, but it looks an expensive way in,&quot; said one analyst who declined to be named.</p>
<p>Elsewhere in the sector, Royal Sun Alliance put on 6-1/2p to 460p, Guardian Royal 3-1/2p to 278-1/2p and General Accident 5-1/2p to 902p.</p>
<p>CU put on 2.36 percent while the FTSE 100 was 0.68 percent higher.</p>
<p>-- Louise Ireland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
</text>
